(7523629, 1202257, 124190, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyClick:</b></div><hr/><i> Hi Viv,<br/> <br/>I''ll comment on the moth that''s attracted to the flowers.  Good catch! <br/> <br/>I was "introduced" to this interesting creature when one visited our Buddliea blooms last year.  They have a really unusual movement. I had no idea what I was seeing at first. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1185389" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2327/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1185389.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2327/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1185389.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2327/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1185389.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Penny!    Yes, don''t they!? I thought I was seeing a baby hummingbird, the first time I saw one.   This year I have some that are actually bright red and green imitating the hummingbird colors and others that are rather tan and brown.   How are you!!!</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyClick: Hi Viv, I''ll comment on the moth that''s attracted to the flowers.  Good catch!  I was "introduced" to this interesting creature when one visited our Buddliea blooms last year.  They have a really unusual movement. I had no idea what I was seeing at first.     Hi Penny!    Yes, don''t they!? I thought I was seeing a baby hummingbird, the first time I saw one.   This year I have some that are actually bright red and green imitating the hummingbird colors and others that are rather tan and brown.   How are you!!!', '2017-07-15 14:47:50.000000', NULL, 0),
